data: {"type":"response.output_text.done","sequence_number":1506,"item_id":"msg_0b0ea63b73509b96016b07aeb0f72c87d1bc37f1178edb425f","output_index":1,"content_index":0,"text":"{\"queries\":[],\"result_json\":\"{\\\"reviews\\\":[{\\\"actor\\\":\\\"kai\\\",\\\"decision\\\":\\\"develop\\\",\\\"ability\\\":null,\\\"reason\\\":\\\"Develop general evidence-based thermal food preparation, not a root-specific interface. The related-capability search found unheated-food-preparation and probe: their observation and dry-handling functions are reusable, but neither supplies controlled heating or evidence of detoxification. No equivalent thermal operation was retrieved; the incomplete catalogue is not proof of absence. The development handoff must check implementation-level equivalents and record reused IDs and code rather than claim reinvention. Kai currently has no confirmed usable heat source or cooking arrangement, so the immediate executable result is a paid, evidence-limited feasibility inspection, not cooked roots. Missing thermal mechanisms are development dependencies, not grounds for permanent rejection.\\\",\\\"specification\\\":\\\"General operation: assess or thermally prepare an owned food quantity, inspect work, or cancel. Parameters: exact inputStackId, quantity, mode, and, when heating, exact sourceId, support/tool/vessel IDs and recipe/evidence reference if one actually exists. Do not bind the operation to Kai or roots. Reuse probe observation semantics and existing inventory, ageing, ownership, work and event code; reuse unheated-food-preparation handling code only where applicable, without treating brushing as cooking. Before registering a new public capability, reconcile against full registry schemas in the existing development handoff.\\\\nCurrent references: item-60-kai-699 contains 2 owned roots at (15.2,19.3), origin commons-root-1-0; food safety unknown. item-24-kai-281 contains 0.8 branch at (11.4,18.25), not automatically carried, reachable or usable fuel. item-66-kai-763 contains 2 known-safe berries and is not an implicit cooking input. Source commons-root-1-0 is not owned cooking stock. Resolve live positions, quantity and ownership at execution rather than copying this snapshot.\\\\nMinimal executable precursor: assess costs one active simulation round and 0.2 energy, consumes no food or fuel, and requires the selected item to be within actual observation/handling reach. Report directly observable condition, existing treatment records and which explicitly supplied prerequisites are unverified or absent from the inspected arrangement. Do not search hidden inventory or world resources. The initial result may state that no usable heat source or cooking arrangement has been demonstrated; it must not claim none exists anywhere. A failed precondition check costs no material or energy and performs no work. Assessment never labels the roots edible or cooked.\\\\nThermal mode requires an actual reachable heat source, a physically workable means of exposing and retrieving the selected food without unsupported safe bare-hand contact, and any method-specific tools, food-contact surface, vessel or water. A waterless method need not require a vessel or water if an actual supported arrangement exists. Ignition is a prerequisite only where the actual heat source requires it; a branch alone supplies neither ignition nor guaranteed fuel suitability. No tasting trial is used to establish safety. Movement, gathering, acquisition, ignition and communication remain separate actual actions, not free substeps.\\\\nImplement missing heat-transfer/source support in this same development handoff if no reusable mechanism exists. Until that support is executable, assessment remains available and heating reports the specific dependency unavailable, without charging a heating round. Do not invent a facility, fire, recipe or sequence of future unlocks. The heating dependency must define simulation-round duration, resource mass/thermal properties, source output, fuel consumption, transfer losses and exposure geometry before enabling thermal mode. These must be explicit versioned code constants or measured represented inputs, not model guesses on each call. No successful cooking claim from an arbitrary fixed timer.\\\\nHeating costs one active round and 0.5 actor energy per supervised work round, plus measured source energy and actual fuel consumed under that source's published code. Setup and safe removal each require one active round and 0.5 energy when physically applicable. Reserve, do not duplicate, the selected quantity. Log elapsed exposure and delivered heat each round, conserving source energy into food, apparatus and environmental losses. Fuel becomes represented combustion products and residues according to the source model; water loss becomes vapor, food loss becomes residue or waste. Preserve original food identity, origin, age, decay, untreated hazards and quantity accounting through splits. Report measured heating, softening, drying, scorching or spoilage only when modeled and actually reached. Never reset decay, grant nutrition, remove toxins or infer edibility merely from heating. A validated processing rule may change a particular hazard only when its exact evidence reference, food applicability and required conditions are met; otherwise safety remains unknown. Eating uses eat separately with actual nutrition and toxicity.\\\\nPersist work ID, input and apparatus references, reserved quantities, mode, accumulated active rounds, exposure, temperature where represented, consumption, observations and status. Recheck ownership, reach, energy and physical prerequisites before each charge. An unworked round or lost prerequisite pauses actor work without an extra work charge; passive heat transfer, ageing, combustion and hazards continue only through their real ongoing process rules. Pause is not automatic safe removal or extinguishing. Resume rechecks current arrangement and continues from actual state, not from a pristine input. Cancel costs one round and no actor energy, stops further intentional handling, releases reservations once and leaves food, hot apparatus and source in their actual locations and states. Death ends personal work and releases reservations without teleporting items or extinguishing a fire. Completed changes and consumed fuel/time/energy are never refunded; unused material is retained, not recreated. No maintenance is free: additional fuel, source tending and safe repositioning require actual inputs and actions. After implementation, established validation, progress, effects and lifecycle rules execute in code without repeated model review. Review/development waiting advances no simulation time.\\\",\\\"learning\\\":3,\\\"experienceReview\\\":\\\"Three individual study rounds confer access only after implementation, not mastery, food, heat or experiential reward. No benefit for requesting, assessment invocation, naming, registration, blocked prerequisites or merely reading a missing-equipment list. A genuinely new, personally observed and verified result, including informative failure, may qualify under the existing experience ledger; deduplicate by underlying finding and conditions across probe and preparation. This capability creates no independent reward payout, satisfaction meter, nutrition bonus or guaranteed comfort. Any later legitimate practice benefit must use existing event-based caps, decay and cooldown rules; if no applicable coded rule exists, award none. Physical comfort remains capped at 10, and basic nutrition is not mood-scaled. Protected reward accounts, budget, goals and permissions remain unchanged.\\\",\\\"visualReview\\\":\\\"Emit reusable structured events only for actual assessment, setup, exposure, measured change, pause, resume, cancellation, completion or failure. Include work ID, actor, exact input/output/source references, position, simulation time, quantities, actual treatment, evidence references, safety status and failure reason. Reusable visual metadata should distinguish raw/unchanged, heating, heated-but-safety-unknown, scorched, paused and dependency-blocked states. Show flame, steam, glow or changed food appearance only when corresponding physical events occurred. A feasibility result may display an observation record and missing-prerequisite indicator, never a cooked-food icon or success animation. Thermal completion means only the specified observed thermal treatment completed; neither its label nor appearance certifies edibility.\\\"}]}\"}","logprobs":[]}

